         <div type="translation" xml:lang="en">
            <ab xml:lang=" en">
               <pb n="" />
               <lb n="1" />To Milon, praktor of the temples. <lb n="2" />A memorandum from Pinyris, son of Estphenis, and Psintaes <lb n="3" />Junior, son of Estphenis. a) Considering that it happened that our one field was given (away) against repayment, <lb n="4" />which is situated in Psebtomit in the nome of Edfou, (and) which represents 30 aruras of field, because <lb n="5" />our payment was agreed for giving concerning Estphenis, son of Pinyris, for the rest, <lb n="6" />which became his burden concerning byssus and the temple disposal of the 23rd regnal year <lb n="7" />[and (concerning)] Berenebthis, son of Estphenis for the same value of byssus <lb n="8" />of the 2nd and 19th regnal year, also his rest; b) (and considering that it happened) [that] it (scil. the field) was given away against repayment, in order to complete 16 silver (deben): <lb n="9" />Thus we may request from you: Considering that it happened <lb n="10"
                   />[that] we have paid our amounts of money together with their interest rate with cash to the bank <lb n="11a" />of Pharaoh within 60 days according to the order <lb n="11b" />of Pharaoh, <lb n="12" />so it is fine, if you may do (the following): Compose in our presence a letter <lb n="13" />of fixtures and fittings in order that it may happen. If that will happen, than we shall not have been damaged. <lb n="14" />Issued by Estphenis, son of Pinyris. 25th regnal year, 19th of Paophi. <lb n="15" />Countersigned by Pinyris, son of Estph[enis]. <lb n="16" />Countersigned by Berenebthis, son of Estphenis. <lb n="17" />[Countersigned by Psintaes, son] of Es- <lb n="18" />-tphenis. </ab>
         </div>
